# S15s: the game's very first view, in the slop preset as it ships. S15c's view: native
# 1920x1080, horizontal plus (id's 90 degrees widened), the status bar scaled and
# overlaid, the gun, `crosshair 1` (it sits on the far teleporter's NORMAL plaque), a
# frame every refresh (`clock free`), the mixer at 48000 Hz, Brightness 0.8. 23 s with a
# second of handle each end, on S15c's clock.
#
# Under V3-08, "This is quake-srp: the slop rust port. Quake, ported to Rust by AI
# agents.", and V3-09, "By default, it is the same renderer, given a twenty twenty-six
# machine." (S15); S16 opens on it under V4-11, "Switch them all off, and you get Classic:
# id's game."
#
# Assembly (S15, S16): S15 is S15s alone from file second 1.0. S16 takes both files from
# file second 19.0 (the camera never moves, so the later frames show the same view): it
# opens on S15s, black pillars close in to the 4:3 box over 0.4 s (eased), and on the
# closed box the picture is S15c, with the edit's "Classic" label at the box's top left
# and id's menu sound on the switch.

map start

duration 25
fps 60
size 1920x1080

preset slop
crosshair 1
hud on
gun on
cvar gamma 0.8

camera player

sound on
events on
